{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"S-near\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The passage moves from third-person praise to the doubled direct address in إِيَّاكَ, then turns that address into a shared request for direction.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:2\",\"ar\":\"ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:4\",\"ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The shift from naming and describing God in 1:2–4 to إِيَّاكَ in 1:5, followed by the plural imperative in 1:6, makes praise into collective address and petition.\",\"limits\":\"The sequence establishes a change in discourse, but does not name the speakers or state that the request is a consequence of their service.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-baseline_exclusive_service_and_support\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The clauses can sound like a commitment to exclusive service followed by a request for the support that would sustain it; the next verse specifies guidance as a need.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"}],\"missing\":\"The conjunction links the clauses but does not state that aid sustains or enables service. A passage that explicitly connects service with aid as its condition or continuation could establish that relation.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-baseline_dependent_agency\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The speakers claim active service in نَعْبُدُ and نَسْتَعِينُ while seeking aid exclusively from the one just named مَٰلِكِ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ: their agency is voiced together with dependence.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:4\",\"ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The first-person plural verbs assert action, while the preceding ownership and the second clause's request for aid deny self-sufficiency.\",\"limits\":\"The text supports dependent action; it does not make the speakers passive or specify how much capacity the aid supplies.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-baseline_honoring_service\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"With the honoring and magnifying sense of ع ب د in view, نَعْبُدُ can present service as active recognition of the one already praised, as well as submission to him.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:2\",\"ar\":\"ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The praise and lordship named before the speakers' service make its honor-giving direction salient.\",\"limits\":\"The sequence supports worship as enacted recognition, but does not establish that magnification displaces submission as the verb's sense.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-delta_named_merciful_address\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The repeated إِيَّاكَ addresses the God already named as ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ, praised as Lord of the worlds, and identified as owner of the day of judgment; the aid request is made within this disclosed relation.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:1\",\"ar\":\"ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:2\",\"ar\":\"رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:4\",\"ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The opening names and describes the addressee before the second-person pronoun recurs in the service and aid clauses.\",\"limits\":\"The context identifies the addressee and his attributes; it does not specify a particular merciful form of aid.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-delta_enclosed_dependency\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The mercy words in the opening could be heard through their relation to رَحِم, “womb,” recasting dependence as life held and formed within a sustaining enclosure.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:3\",\"ar\":\"ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"}],\"missing\":\"Surah 1 names mercy but contains no womb, gestation, or formation image. A lexical attestation of this association together with a Quranic passage that activates womb imagery alongside sustaining dependence could establish the extension.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-delta_agency_without_self_credit\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ precedes the speakers' own نَعْبُدُ, and their subsequent request for aid lets the service be voiced as a real deed without claiming its ultimate praise or capacity for themselves.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:2\",\"ar\":\"ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"}],\"activation\":\"Praise is assigned to God before the speakers announce their action, and the aid clause follows their service claim.\",\"limits\":\"The order and aid request suggest dependence, but the passage does not explicitly deny the speakers credit for their deed.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-delta_formed_for_service\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ immediately precedes service and a request for aid, allowing the need for help to be heard as formative as well as immediate.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:2\",\"ar\":\"رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"}],\"missing\":\"The passage does not say that the speakers are being repaired, nourished, or formed for service. A Quranic use of رَبّ that explicitly describes formation or growth in connection with service could supply that support.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-delta_covenantal_pair\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The first clause can sound like a pledge of exclusive service and the second like a request for the backing needed to keep it, giving the pair a possible compact-like shape.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"}],\"missing\":\"No pact or covenant term, condition, or exchange appears here. A passage that explicitly pairs a service pledge with requested aid as a compact could establish this framing.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-delta_accountable_obedience\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Placed after مَٰلِكِ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ, exclusive service is heard under an horizon of reckoning; seeking aid can then sound like dependence in carrying out that accountable service.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:4\",\"ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The judgment and recompense phrase directly precedes the speakers' service and aid request.\",\"limits\":\"The sequence supplies the accountability horizon, but does not explicitly say that aid is sought for endurance until judgment.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-delta_service_as_path_work\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The material smoothing sense associated with ع ب د can make نَعْبُدُ resonate as treading or making a route passable, immediately before the request for ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The path and its straightness are explicit in the next verse, activating the proposed route sense of the service root.\",\"limits\":\"Surah 1 does not use ع ب د to mean road-paving; this is a contextual lexical resonance, not a replacement translation.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-delta_maintained_uprightness\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Because نَسْتَعِينُ is followed by ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ, the aid request can include help in keeping service oriented on a straight path, rather than help only in a moment of incapacity.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The next verse immediately makes guidance toward a straight path the specific petition after seeking aid.\",\"limits\":\"The passage does not explicitly call aid continuous preservation or correction; that maintenance sense is inferred from the sequence.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-delta_help_as_gift_not_wage\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The next request names guidance, and the path is later identified with those whom God has favored; this frames guidance as benefaction that enables service rather than as a wage claimed for it.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:7\",\"ar\":\"ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ\"}],\"activation\":\"The prayer for guidance leads into a description of its path through the people who received divine favor.\",\"limits\":\"The passage presents guidance alongside benefaction but does not explicitly reject a transactional account of every form of aid.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-delta_servitude_softened_by_benefaction\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"If نَعْبُدُ is heard through an ownership or servitude register, the following reference to those favored by God places benefaction alongside that asymmetry.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:7\",\"ar\":\"ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ\"}],\"missing\":\"The passage does not describe coercion, ease, or a change from coercion to benefaction. A Quranic occurrence joining service language with explicit markers of coercion or care could decide how far this contrast carries.\",\"support\":\"weak\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-delta_exclusivity_as_drift_resistance\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The repeated إِيَّاكَ fixes one addressee, and the following request for the straight path with its two excluded outcomes frames that exclusivity as resistance to losing direction.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:7\",\"ar\":\"غَيْرِ ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا ٱلضَّآلِّينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus verse's repeated exclusive object is followed by a shared request for guidance and a contrast with angered and astray groups.\",\"limits\":\"The text supports steadiness of direction but does not identify a specific substituted deity or say that the angered group actively opposes God.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-delta_collective_recoherence\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The plural speakers address one addressee, seek aid together, and ask for one path; the utterance gathers its speakers around a shared direction.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:7\",\"ar\":\"صِرَٰطَ ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ\"}],\"activation\":\"Plural first-person forms converge on a singular exclusive object and a shared path.\",\"limits\":\"The grammar performs collective orientation, but the passage does not establish that the speakers were previously scattered or divided.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-outlier_watchful_eye_aid\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The aid request might also carry an image of sustained protective attention if the cited ع و ن branch of watchful care is active here.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:1\",\"ar\":\"ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"}],\"missing\":\"The surah names mercy and requested aid but contains no word for seeing or watching. A passage co-activating this aid sense with vigilance, or further lexical evidence for its relevance to this form, could establish the attentive-care reading.\",\"support\":\"weak\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-outlier_present_provision_against_debt\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The debt sense of ٱلدِّينِ beside the request for aid allows a secondary image of dependent servants seeking present provision against an approaching obligation.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:4\",\"ar\":\"مَٰلِكِ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"}],\"missing\":\"No money, payment, or material need is named, and يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ is framed here as a day. A Quranic use joining the debt sense of د ي ن with tangible provision or requested aid could establish the economic image.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-outlier_obstacle_breaking_guidance\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"A proposed removal or demolition sense associated with ه د ي could make the aid request evoke opening a blocked route, with the next verse supplying the path image.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"}],\"missing\":\"The surah names guidance and a path but no obstruction or removal. A lexical attestation for that sense in the relevant form and a Quranic passage where guidance removes a barrier could activate this reading.\",\"support\":\"weak\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-outlier_seasoned_conflict_backing\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"Exclusive service and aid followed by the contrast with angered and astray groups could be heard as allegiance under pressure, but the conflict setting remains hypothetical here.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:7\",\"ar\":\"غَيْرِ ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا ٱلضَّآلِّينَ\"}],\"missing\":\"The surah names adverse outcomes but no recurring struggle or retaliation. A related Quranic scene pairing this service-and-aid formula with an explicit conflict would establish the setting.\",\"support\":\"weak\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}"}}
